{"nodes": [{"id": "setup_path_a_docker", "label": "Path A \u2014 Docker install", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "SETUP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Isolated container, no system changes, easy to throw away \u2014 chosen for 'I just want to try it'."}, {"id": "setup_path_b_native", "label": "Path B \u2014 Native install (local or SSH box)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "SETUP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Local and SSH variants run identical steps; native is chosen when the box should be an always-on agent host with full host access for agents."}, {"id": "setup_setup_wizard", "label": "First-open setup wizard (/setup)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "SETUP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Four steps (Welcome, Agents, Connectivity, Done) so credentials, the Telegram token and a public URL can be configured without editing .env by hand. Personal assistants are deliberately excluded from onboarding."}, {"id": "setup_auto_pairing", "label": "Trust-on-first-connect auto-pairing", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "SETUP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The first browser to reach a fresh instance is trusted and paired with no extra step, removing all friction on a local install; on headless or already-exposed boxes `bun run pair <name>` mints an explicit pairing URL instead."}, {"id": "setup_env_file", "label": "~/.mux/state/.env broker env file", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "SETUP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The web channel activates as soon as MUX_WEB_PORT and MUX_WEB_PUBLIC_URL are both set; no Telegram token is required. With the relay on, MUX_WEB_PUBLIC_URL can stay localhost because `supermux pair` publishes the stable relay URL instead."}, {"id": "setup_systemd_user_service", "label": "systemd user service (supermux.service)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "SETUP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A user (not system) service keeps the broker inside the user's own session and environment; `loginctl enable-linger` is REQUIRED on an SSH-managed box or every session dies when the SSH connection ends."}, {"id": "setup_expose_port_modes", "label": "expose_port: subdomain mode vs path mode", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "SETUP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Subdomain mode (MUX_PROXY_BASE_DOMAIN set) gives each app its own origin but needs wildcard DNS + wildcard TLS. Path mode needs neither but strips /p/<slug> before forwarding, so apps assuming a domain root (absolute /asset links, fetch('/api'), Vite/Next dev servers) break, and all path-exposed apps share the broker origin so localStorage/IndexedDB are NOT isolated between them."}, {"id": "setup_cloudflare_tunnel", "label": "Cloudflare Tunnel (quick vs named)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "SETUP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A quick tunnel is zero-config but its URL changes on every cloudflared restart, and a new URL means re-pairing every device \u2014 so only a named tunnel is suitable for a box you intend to keep."}, {"id": "setup_done_checklist", "label": "\"You're done when\u2026\" acceptance checklist", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "SETUP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "setu